## 📊 1. INVESTIGATOR FIELD OBSERVATIONS

Gravity and center of balance and micro-movement.

I noticed that when I planted my feet and I turned my upper body, and I tried to contract myself, I think like a worm, by like pulling—or like tensing and pulling—my body with my skin and muscles, it felt like certain parts of my back near the spine. It started feeling like it was like I was like wearing like a padded suit or something. Most of that feeling has gone away; it was—it’s only on my left side though, but I can still feel like it’s tense, but it’s not tense.

On the actual ex—or the amount of time that it took to actually put my body back into shape, even though my eyes were closed and my brain thought that I was still turned, but my body was upright and aligned. It took like a few minutes.

I’m also noticing that the center of gravity is like weird if I stand upright and I lock my knees just a little bit, it feels like it’s like my entire back.

